Configuration — part of this SOUP record (NP-SOUP-LFS-001 §7.3).
The build-time configuration and the per-instance parameters are NeurOne-authored
and are NOT part of the vendored component.  They live with the hub control
program, on the FreeRTOSConfig.h precedent (one owner, one source of truth):
  firmware/hub_control/include/np_lfs_config.h    — build-time configuration,
                                                    reached via -DLFS_DEFINES
  firmware/hub_control/include/np_lfs_instance.h  — EMMC-FS-01 instance
  firmware/hub_control/src/np_lfs_instance.c        parameters + the mount-time
                                                    validator
  firmware/hub_control/tests/np_lfs_config_tests.c  — the host test that asserts
                                                    both against this record

Build-time configuration in force (np_lfs_config.h; read it for the reasoning):
  LFS_DEFINES=np_lfs_config.h  the ONE compile definition.  Everything else is
                       set inside that header rather than on a command line, so
                       a translation unit that includes lfs.h cannot see a
                       different configuration from the one lfs.c was built
                       with.  LFS_THREADSAFE changes the layout of struct
                       lfs_config, so that is a correctness property, not tidiness.
  LFS_NO_MALLOC        static allocation.  The device's heap is a fixed 64 KiB
                       FreeRTOS pool and filesystem buffers must not come from
                       it.  With this set, lfs_malloc() returns NULL, so a
                       caller that forgets a buffer gets LFS_ERR_NOMEM at mount
                       rather than a working filesystem on borrowed heap.
  LFS_ASSERT(...)      assertions stay ON, retargeted.  NeurOne's handler halts
                       the main processor, which stops the SPI heartbeat, which
                       makes the safety MCU cut all stimulation within <50 ms
                       (CLAUDE.md §4.2).  Compiling a Class B filesystem with
                       its internal invariants disabled is the alternative, and
                       it is not one: lfs_init()'s configuration checks are
                       assertions.
  LFS_NO_ASSERT        deliberately NOT defined — and it is the obvious-looking
                       companion to the line above, so the reason is recorded
                       rather than left to be rediscovered.  Upstream reads it
                       as "assertions are compiled out", not as "do not include
                       <assert.h>": lfs.c:507 guards the DEFINITION of
                       lfs_mlist_isopen with it while lfs.c:6178 keeps the CALL
                       inside LFS_ASSERT.  Setting both gives an implicit
                       declaration and then an undefined symbol at link — and
                       only once something pulls lfs.o in.  Found by building
                       it.  Patching the vendored file is not available
                       (NP-SW-CI-001 §9), so the configuration yields; the cost
                       is one unused <assert.h> include.  Note what the
                       assertion in question checks: that a file is not already
                       open through a SECOND HANDLE — the exact condition behind
                       the corruption defect this tag was pinned for.
  LFS_NO_DEBUG,        the three logging families are OFF, which also removes
  LFS_NO_WARN,         lfs_util.h's <stdio.h> include.  CLAUDE.md §17: firmware
  LFS_NO_ERROR         renders no text at all.  A printf here would be both dead
                       code and a locale boundary the firmware does not have.
  LFS_THREADSAFE       ON.  lfs_config gains lock/unlock, and the validator
                       REFUSES a config whose lock or unlock is NULL — with
                       this define a NULL lock is a call through a null pointer
                       on the first API call, so the check is the difference
                       between a rejected mount and a hard fault.
  LFS_MULTIVERSION     NOT defined: NeurOne writes the on-disk version of the
                       pinned library (2.1) and reads no foreign media.
  LFS_READONLY         NOT defined: every instance is written.
  LFS_NO_INTRINSICS    NOT defined: the GCC builtins are wanted on Cortex-M7.

