What this vendoring does not establish.  Stated plainly, because a directory
appearing under firmware/vendor/ reads as "integrated" and this one is not yet:
  - NOTHING CALLS IT.  np_log_backend.h's OI-LOG-05..07 seams are still
    unimplemented; np_littlefs is built and linked into no image.  `grep -rn
    "lfs_" firmware/ --include=*.c --include=*.h` outside this directory and the
    NeurOne configuration files above still finds no call.
  - L-1..L-4 are exercised against the CONTRACT, not the medium (OI-LFS-07).
    NP-FW-NVRAM-001 §4 and NP-FW-HUB-001 §6.5 may be relied on exactly that far
    and no further — NP-SOUP-LFS-001 §12.5 states the boundary.  Note also that
    L-3's result is a property of the write-temp-then-rename ORDERING the test
    swept, not of this component: littlefs does not make a replacement atomic,
    that ordering does, and the OI-LOG-05..07 glue has to use it.
  - Wear levelling (L-6) is configured, never measured.  block_cycles 500 is set
    and checked by value; nothing observes its effect, and on managed flash it
    may not mean what the claim assumes (OI-LFS-07).
  - Only the Config instance has parameters.  The UHDR and SHDR log partitions
    carry claims L-1 and L-2 and NO document states their instance parameters —
    raised as OI-LFS-05 by NP-SOUP-LFS-001 Rev 2.
